{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'cat ../research.json'","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"audit_spec_path\": \"/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-04_17-36-49-etcd_raft-real-run/audit-spec/v1.json\",\n  \"audit_spec_version\": 1,\n  \"activity_roles\": {\n    \"A1\": {\n      \"role\": \"core\",\n      \"relation\": \"Qualified support for decision formation and legal advancement\"\n    },\n    \"A2\": {\n      \"role\": \"core\",\n      \"relation\": \"Context validity and acquisition, transfer or loss of authority\"\n    },\n    \"A3\": {\n      \"role\": \"support\",\n      \"relation\": \"Recovery and resynchronization of eligible participation\"\n    },\n    \"A4\": {\n      \"role\": \"support\",\n      \"relation\": \"Configuration and participant eligibility\"\n    },\n    \"A5\": {\n      \"role\": \"support\",\n      \"relation\": \"Decision application and consumption\"\n    },\n    \"A6\": {\n      \"role\": \"support\",\n      \"relation\": \"History, persistence and reconstruction of support\"\n    },\n    \"A7\": {\n      \"role\": \"support\",\n      \"relation\": \"Client contracts, invocation intervals and observed completion\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"activity_focus\": [],\n  \"understanding_status\": \"usable\",\n  \"core_overview\": {\n    \"formation\": {\n      \"explanation\": \"A caller proposes through RawNode/Node. The leader assigns term/index, appends unstable entries and replicates with predecessor identity. Followers require matching predecessor, refuse committed conflicts, and queue append replies after persistence. The leader self-acks after its persistence completion and aggregates peer Match using active voter majority (both halves for joint configuration); only a quorum index in its current term directly advances commitment. Append messages and Match-capped heartbeats propagate commitment. Ready exposes committed work; the caller applies entries in order and applies configuration entries. Advance or async application replies account for completion. Rejections probe backward, heartbeats reopen flow control, and compacted history uses snapshots.\",\n      \"behavior_ids\": [\n        \"b_formation\",\n        \"b_persistence\",\n        \"b_application\",\n        \"b_recovery\"\n      ],\n      \"fact_ids\": [\n        \"f_commit\"\n      ],\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"s_send\",\n        \"s_replication_send\",\n        \"s_ack\",\n        \"s_log_matching\",\n        \"s_apply_completion\",\n        \"s_proposal_read\",\n        \"s_reset_append\",\n        \"s_log_append\",\n        \"s_tracker\",\n        \"s_joint\",\n        \"s_majority\",\n        \"s_ready_contract\",\n        \"s_ready\",\n        \"s_append_completion\",\n        \"s_dispatch\",\n        \"s_stable\",\n        \"s_storage_contract\",\n        \"s_log_apply\",\n        \"s_log_commit_apply\",\n        \"s_applied\",\n        \"s_node_contract\",\n        \"s_init\",\n        \"s_recovery\",\n        \"s_transfer\",\n        \"s_config\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"context\": {\n      \"explanation\": \"A promotable node with no unapplied committed configuration changes campaigns, optionally with pre-vote. Votes require eligible vote state and an up-to-date candidate log; configured voter quorums determine election. Term dispatch rejects stale replies and usually steps down on higher terms, with pre-vote/lease exceptions. Reset clears vote aggregation, replication progress, read-only heartbeat support and transfer state while preserving the committed prefix. Storage replies are term-scoped for entry stabilization, but committed snapshot/application completion survives term changes. Transfer suppresses proposals until success, abort or timeout. Applied configuration changes alter voter eligibility; snapshots/restart restore membership and history.\",\n      \"behavior_ids\": [\n        \"b_authority\",\n        \"b_transfer\",\n        \"b_membership\",\n        \"b_recovery\"\n      ],\n      \"fact_ids\": [\n        \"f_joint\"\n      ],\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"s_ticks_roles\",\n        \"s_campaign\",\n        \"s_dispatch\",\n        \"s_config\",\n        \"s_recovery\",\n        \"s_follow_roles\",\n        \"s_reset_append\",\n        \"s_votes\",\n        \"s_joint\",\n        \"s_majority\",\n        \"s_log_matching\",\n        \"s_transfer\",\n        \"s_abort\",\n        \"s_proposal_read\",\n        \"s_changer\",\n        \"s_conf_invariants\",\n        \"s_conf_contract\",\n        \"s_joint_contract\",\n        \"s_conf_decode\",\n        \"s_init\",\n        \"s_replication_send\",\n        \"s_log_append\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"connection\": {\n      \"explanation\": \"The term and active configuration jointly qualify support: a leader consumes only current-context responses from tracked participants, while quorum evaluation selects voters and joint majorities. Membership application can reinterpret existing Match and advance commitment without a new reply. A new leader resets remote Match, appends a new-term empty entry, and cannot campaign past known unapplied configuration changes. Pending read heartbeat support is reset, but the separate pre-commit read queue survives reset. Applying a joint configuration sets AutoLeave; application completion may propose its exit, while concurrent transfer may reject that proposal. Established decisions remain a prefix through authority changes; persistence and application completion have distinct response rules.\",\n      \"behavior_ids\": [\n        \"b_formation\",\n        \"b_authority\",\n        \"b_persistence\",\n        \"b_application\",\n        \"b_membership\",\n        \"b_transfer\",\n        \"b_recovery\",\n        \"b_reads\"\n      ],\n      \"fact_ids\": [\n        \"f_commit\",\n        \"f_joint\"\n      ],\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"s_reset_append\",\n        \"s_campaign\",\n        \"s_config\",\n    