om generic proposal semantics.\"\n        ],\n        \"unknowns\": [\n          \"Whether the documented implicit exit responsibility requires retry without further client proposals after a failed transfer.\",\n          \"Whether a legal producer history can leave no pending application work when the transfer aborts.\",\n          \"Whether timers, duplicate responses, configuration events or other internal paths retry independently of a later applied entry.\"\n        ],\n        \"priority\": 2,\n        \"trigger_rationale\": \"The implicit-transition API assigns exit to Raft. appliedTo explicitly admits transfer rejection and relies on a next advance, while abortLeaderTransfer only clears a field. Inspect all callers and pending-work production before choosing a controlled execution; this is more discriminating than testing already composed durability guards or the ReadIndex path whose caller retry duty is explicit.\"\n      },\n      \"status\": \"active\",\n      \"parent_candidate_id\": null,\n      \"fork_reason\": \"\",\n      \"stop_reason\": \"Establish both core relationships and retain a sourced continuation question before claiming an obligation or running a check.\",\n      \"resume_conditions\": [],\n      \"obligation_id\": null,\n      \"result_claim_ids\": [],\n      \"open_issue_ids\": [],\n      \"executions\": [],\n      \"record\": {\n        \"path\": \"state.json\",\n        \"collection\": \"question_candidates\",\n        \"match\": {\n          \"id\": \"584b72abffa84bc88a7de31800f4271d\"\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  ],\n  \"units\": [],\n  \"claims\": [],\n  \"artifacts\": [],\n  \"assessments\": [],\n  \"frontier\": {\n    \"relationships\": [\n      {\n        \"fact_id\": \"f_commit\",\n        \"source_ids\": [\n          \"s_init\",\n          \"s_log_matching\",\n          \"s_log_append\",\n          \"s_replication_send\",\n          \"s_recovery\",\n          \"s_config\"\n        ],\n        \"unknowns\": [],\n        \"prod